N2  - Pancreatic carcinoma is a common malignancy of gastrointestinal system. Multi-department and multi-center combined therapy has great developments in many areas, including surgery, chemotherapy, radiotherapy, physical, biological-therapy and so on. Surgical management is a major therapy, including radical operation and palliative operation. Rational operation could improve the patients' long-term survival rate and the quality of life. Radiotherapy includes accessory irradiation combined with operation and palliative irradiation. Preoperational radiotherapy and chemotherapy could improve resectional rate of operation and decrease the tumor dissemination. Intraoperation irradiation includes intraoperative electron radiation therapy, intraoperative radiational practical implantment and so on. It could relieve pain and enhance survival rate, but the effect of post-operation adjuvant radiotherapy is still controversial. Chemotherapy consists of intravenous chemotherapy and regional chemotherapy, combined chemotherapy couldn't significantly prolong the survival term of patients with pancreatic carcinoma compared with single chemotherapy. Regional chemotherapy is selective artery administration and has many advantages in theory. Physical and biological-therapy also get widely recommendations. But only combined therapy consisting of surgical resection, radiotherapy, chemotherapy, physical and biological-therapy could increase the long-term survival rates and improve the life quality of the patients with pancreatic carcinoma.
