N2  - Promising preclinical data regarding the combination of EGFR inhibitors with radiation therapy have led to a series of new clinical studies. The potential value of this approach was recently validated by an international phase III clinical trial, which showed that the addition of cetuximab (Erbitux™) to radiation therapy in patients with advanced head and neck cancer produced a significant survival advantage versus radiation therapy alone. An expanding cohort of clinical trials that combine EGFR inhibitors (monoclonal antibodies and tyrosine kinase inhibitors) with radiation therapy are under way in other treatment settings and cancer types. In addition to confirming the efficacy and tolerability of such approaches, it will be important to identify those specific patient populations most likely to obtain clinical benefit. This review discusses the preclinical and clinical data obtained to date in this rapidly advancing field of clinical research. © 2005 Adis International Limited.
