N2  - We report a patient with gastric carcinoma successfully treated with TS-1/CDDP as a neoadjuvant chemotherapy. The patient was a 72-year-old man who had suffered from general malaise with severe anemia and was diagnosed as type 2 carcinoma, having bulky N2, with suspected invasion of the pancreas. TS-1 (100 mg/day) was administered orally every day for 21 days followed by 14 days rest, and CDDP (20 mg/body) was administered by intravenous infusion at day 8, as one course. He was treated as an outpatient, and two courses of treatment resulted in a marked reduction of the lymphnode metastasis without toxicity. Subsequently, he underwent curative surgery consisting of total gastrectomy with D2 lymph node dissection. TS-1/CDDP therapy is very useful as a neoadjuvant chemotherapy especially for an outpatient until surgery.
