N2  - This 2-day meeting was an excellent opportunity to discuss both European and US approaches to the treatment of GI tract cancer. Major differences in the US and European approaches include the use of infused and bolus 5-FU/LV, treatments of rectal cancer, the emphasis on TME and preoperative short-term irradiation in Europe, and more postoperative standard chemoradiotherapy in US. In addition there is more postoperative chemoradiotherapy in resected pancreatic and gastric cancer in the USA. Challenging cases in colorectal cancer and gastric cancer were presented by Dr Jacques Wils and Dr J Macdonald. There was a voting system to provide optimal interchange with the audience and after each lecture one slide was presented that showed questions concerning a typical case with different possible approaches (eg, How would you, treat this patient?).
