N2  - In order to improve the results of surgery for pancreatic cancer, different adjuvant treatment regimens have been investigated during the last two decades. Three randomized trials on adjuvant chemoradiation have been published leading to controverse results. But, about 25% of the patients never have received any adjuvant therapy due to complicated postoperative course after Whipple's procedure. Early studies using preoperative chemoradiation only included patients with locally advanced, unresectable but non-metastatic pancreatic cancer. Recently, preoperative chemoradiation has been introduced in resectable pancreatic cancer. The major advantage of neoadjuvant treatment is, that all patients receive a combined modality treatment. We introduce a new multimodality approach to resectable pancreatic cancer, which is currently investigated at the University Hospital of Zurich.
