N2  - Despite the long natural history and the effectiveness of screening programs for early detection, GI cancer is frequently diagnosed at an advanced stage. Surgery, radiotherapy, but mainly chemotherapy are claimed to treat the disease. Several antiproliferative drugs are available. Up today, among patients with advanced cancer, only a few number gain a satisfactory post-chemotherapy level of survival. On the contrary, adjuvant settings and some preoperative strategies show satisfying results. New substances, such as vaccines or anti-angiogenetic factors, are currently under study.
