N2  - Pancreatic tumors have a very bad prognosis even after complete surgery. Radiotherapy has an important role to play either postoperative with associated chemotherapy or palliative and alone. Presently 5-FU is the most widely used molecule but gemcitabine is getting more and more acceptance. Intraoperative radiotherapy but especially preoperative radiotherapy seem to be two promising techniques.
