N2  - A case of 18-year-old man with Borrmann 4-type gastric carcinoma was presented. The patient consulted a physician due to epigastralgia in hungry, and in upper gastrointestinal series a small ulecrative lesion of stomach was found. After a month of medication of anti-ulceratives without any improvements of the symptom, he visited the Department of Surgery, Cancer Research Institute Hospital, Kanazawa University. With X-ray and endoscopic examinations of the stomach, Borrmann 4-type gastric carcinoma was detected. After neoadjuvant chemotherapy, total gastrectomy with resections of pancreatic body and transverse colon was performed. Histopathologically, the cancer measuring 10 x 8 cm was composed of poorly defferentiated adenocarcinoma cells scatterd in desmoplastic stroma. The cancer cells invaded to the transverse colon with lymphatic and vascular involvements. Intraoperative cytology of ascites was positive for malignancy and the operation was noncurative. After a year of the operation, metastasis of liver and kidney appeared and the patient died with peritonitis carcinomatosa. Twenty-five cases of gastric carcinoma of the young in the age from 16 to 19 years were reviewed in the literature. The discussion was made briefly on the clinicopathology of the gastric carcinoma in the young, the necessity of endoscopic examination for the detection of cancer in its early stage was concluded.
