N2  - We report a case of malignant fibrous histiocytoma (MFH) arising from the renal capsule. A 66-year-old man was admitted with the chief complaint of loss of appetite, weight loss, fever and abdominal mass. He was diagnosed as suffering from left renal carcinoma by preoperative radiological examinations. Radical nephrectomy, splenectomy, pancreas tail resection and partial descending colectomy were performed due to tumor invasions on 22 Jan., 1991. The histopathological diagnosis was MFH arising from the renal capsule. Intramuscular injections of IFN-α were tried as an adjuvant therapy, but these were terminated due to the side effect of fever. At his 2-month postoperative examination, CT scan revealed local recurrence. Combination chemotherapy of adriamycin and cyclophosphamide was tried, but this was terminated due to melena. He died on 10th May, 1991. We reviewed 27 domestic case reports of MFH arising from the kidney.
