N2  - 5-FU oil emulsion (n = 5) or 5-FU dry syrup (n = 4), at a daily dose of 332 mg for 7 days, was administered preoperatively to patients with periampullary carcinoma to evaluate the uptake of 5-FU to regional lymph nodes. In the group given 5-FU oil emulsion, the mean concentration of 5-FU was 293 ± 97 ng/ml (mean ± S.E.D.), and that of the group given dry syrup was 72 ± 20 ng/ml. Although no statistically significant difference was found, 5-FU seemed to reach the regional lymph nodes as an emulsion rather than as an aqueous solution. Preoperative administration of 5-FU emulsion might have some favorable effect on lymph node metastasis and lymph invasion of pancreatic carcinoma.
