N2  - The Working Party was of the opinion that certain investigations were of little or no clinical value in PC and, outside research projects, there was no place for the routine use of serological markers of disease or selective angiography. The emphasis of this brief report is therefore on a streamlining of investigation with increased expertise in ultrasonography diagnosis, as well as ERCP assessment. More wide-spread availability of angiogram enhanced CT scanning is desirable. In the minority group (approximately 15 per cent) considered suitable for surgical resection preoperative cytology should be avoided.
