N2  - Primary malignant tumors originating in the pulmonary artery are extremely rare. It was first described by Mandelstamm in 1923. Since then, 45 cases in the world and 5 cases in Japan have been reported in the literature. A 27-year-old man was admitted to our hospital because of left anterior chest pain, cough, hemoptysis and fever. A preoperative diagnosis of primary pulmonary tumor was made on the basis of pulmonary and bronchial angiographic findings. Radical left pneumonectomy was performed, and a malignant mesenchymoma was confirmed by histological examination. After 6 months of well-being, he was readmitted because of abdominal pain, anorexia and loss of weight. Metastases to stomach, pancreas, small intestine and coeliac lymphnodes were revealed by angiographic and gastrofiberscopic examination. Four months later the patient died of panperitonitis due to the perforation of stomach. Chemotherapy with endoxan and adriamycin had been effective.
