N2  - In 59 patients with cancer of the stomach preoperative concentrated irradiation in a dose of 1800-2000 rad caused the change of the insulin content in the blood plasma, the character of deviation of which from the initial level depended upon the degree of the insular apparatus before treatment. The analysis of glycemic curves after double loading by the glucose according to Shtaub-Traugotte testifies to the decrease of the reserve possibilities of the insular apparatus of the pancreas after therapeutic doses of radiation under the conditions of an increased need of the body in insulin.
