N2  - Using biochemical tests, the authors studied the exocrine function of the pancreas after concentrated preoperative irradiation of gastric carcinoma of stage III-IV. Radiation loads on the pancreas were determined by calculation. It comprised 1800-2000 rad. The authors observed a decrease in the activity of amylase in the urine and blood serum. A rise in the activity of pancreatic lipase and fluctuations in the level of the enzymatic activity of trypsin in the blood serum was observed. The presence of the statistically significant correlation between the studied indices makes it possible to associate these changes with disorders of the exocrine function of the pancreas after therapeutic doses of radiation. The observed changes took place on the 3rd day after the termination of the preoperative irradiation. The level of the activity of lipase and trypsin in the blood serum normalized on the 21st day. A low amylase activity of the blood serum and urine still remains; this is assessed as a partial restoration of the function of the pancreas.
